nt_name (DEPARTMENT_NAME vs OFFER_DEPT_NAME conventions), column_concept_term_code (universal join key), column_concept_enrollment_measures (NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS family), column_concept_year_columns (ACADEMIC_YEAR selection).\n\n### 2. Lineage & Relationships\nGraph traversal confirmed: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED ↔ TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED (joins edge), LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED ↔ ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL (joins edge), IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL ↔ ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL (joins edge), IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL ↔ COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED (joins edge), ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL ↔ COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED (via TERM_CODE per column definitions). All tables belong to their respective concepts listed above.\n\n### 3. Similar-Entity Differences\n- **Department naming**: The task's \"Chemistry department\" maps to `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME` (column definition example: 'Chemistry'); \"Mathematics department\" maps to `COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME` (column definition example: 'Mathematics'). Both are in the same academic value domain per column_concept_department_name; the hint decomposition anchors each phrase to its table.\n- **Enrollment measures**: `LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS` (library records) vs `TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS` (TIP scope). The task explicitly says \"number of enrolled students **in the library subject**\" → LIBRARY table's column. SUPPORTED for library; TIP's column is NOT requested.\n- **Term dimension**: ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL is chosen over ACADEMIC_TERMS per hints (superset coverage; provides ACADEMIC_YEAR + ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC).\n- **Fan-out risk**: LIBRARY ⋈ TIP on TERM_CODE alone is a deliberate cross-join within '2014FA' per the gold decomposition (subquery 1) — this is the specified task shape, matching precedent dw_1165's term-code join style.\n\n### 4. Business Usage\n- LIBRARY/TIP subject tables: consumed by metrics dw_1165, dw_3393, dw_3911, dw_2591 for enrollment window statistics and material-status questions.\n- IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL: consumed by dw_3047, dw_4558, dw_2790 for capacity statistics with `IS_CANCELLED='N'` and `MAX_ENROLLMENT IS NOT NULL` filters.\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL: year attribution in dw_4558, dw_1301.\n\n### 5. Coverage Checklist\nAll Phase 1 entities investigated: 5 tables via `semantic_get` (full columns) + `semantic_graph` neighbors for LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED and IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL; metrics/concepts/column-concepts captured via `semantic_search` descriptions. `mysql_query` attempted 4 times — all failed with access-denied (database unavailable); noted explicitly, no data-level verification possible.\n\n### 6. Recommendation\n**6a.** Use LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED (SUBJECT_TITLE, NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) ⋈ TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED (RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_NAME, OFFER_DEPT_NAME, RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_MIT_ID) on TERM_CODE, filtered to '2014FA' and OFFER_DEPT_NAME='Chemistry'; window MIN with ROWS BETWEEN 3 PRECEDING AND 1 FOLLOWING ordered by RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_MIT_ID; cross-join a Chemistry count subquery; cross-join the IAP/Mathematics rollup (IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL ⋈ ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL ⋈ COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED on TERM_CODE, GROUP BY ... WITH ROLLUP, HAVING SUM(variance) IS NOT NULL).\n\n**6b/6c.** Filters `ENROLLMENT_TYPE='Advance sign-up required'`, `IS_CANCELLED='N'`, `MAX_ENROLLMENT IS NOT NULL` follow the documented IAP coverage caveat (data perspective) and dw_3047/dw_4558 precedents (business perspective); join edges confirmed in the graph (semantic-network perspective). Bare `STDDEV()` per convention. No rounding. SELECT list matches the 10 requested columns in order.\n\n",
